00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.310 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  in a bizarre legal case a michigan  couple is being forced to adopt their  own biological children  after they were born through a surrogate  jordan and tammy meyer's twins were born  two weeks ago today but two judges  denied them the legal rights to the  infants  citing a decades-old anti-surrogacy law  nikki batis has been looking at the very  strange case nikki good morning to you  this is just bizarre  it's really bizarre tony good morning  tammy and jordan meyer were hoping for a  sibling for their two-year-old daughter  when tammy was diagnosed with breast  cancer several years ago  her medical treatment left her unable to  go through another pregnancy  so the couple found a gestational  surrogate to carry  their biological child but now to get  the legal rights to their two-week-old  twins  they have to adopt them and initially i  you know i i thought i'm too young and  there's no way it couldn't be breast  cancer  nearly six years ago tammy myers learned  she was in a battle  for her life my first two questions for  her were  how long do i have and my second  question was  can i have more children can i still  have another baby now tammy and her  husband jordan  are facing a new fight this time for the  rights to their newborn twins  tammy froze her eggs after her breast  cancer diagnosis  she is doing better and in 2019 she and  her husband decided to grow their family  they turned to gestational surrogacy did  you ever  think you would be in the situation you  are having to adopt your own two  children  we really truly didn't believe that  someone could could hear the history  and not give us rights tammy and jordan  found their surrogate lauren vermilia  after posting on facebook  lauren who is married with two children  of her own  live nearby and volunteered to carry the  myers child for free  i lasted my dad's pancreatic cancer 11  years ago and just i know what  cancer can take away from you and just  to be able to  help bring that hope back to somebody  just  really really appealed to me and my  husband soon after  two of the myers embryos were  transferred to lauren they learned they  were having  twins the process was going well until  the couple tried to get legal parental  rights  you were denied the pre-birth rights and  then also jordan you were denied  my rights as a father as well yeah two  judges in kent county michigan dismissed  the myers efforts to be named the legal  parents  they cited michigan's surrogate  parenting act of 1988  which states surrogacy contracts are  void and unenforceable  one judge wrote that there are genuine  concerns about the 1988 act  but those concerns are better left to  the legislative and political arena  i just stopped that's all i could do  i just i don't understand it it doesn't  make any sense ames and ellison myers  were born  january 11th a few weeks premature their  birth certificate names the surrogate  lauren  and her husband as the parents michigan  law states that i am a married woman  and so of course my husband would be the  father  of my children which they're not my  children either  melissa neckers is the myers attorney  she said since 2005  there have been at least 72 cases in  michigan  where judges have granted parents in  similar situations pre-birth legal  rights  to their biological children did they  understand the risk  they faced based not only on michigan's  law but also that they had a stranger as  a gestational carrier  they knew that there was risk but they  really believed that no  judge would actually hear their story  which had  so many additional layers of heartache  and  trauma that a judge wouldn't just want  to do the right thing  only two other states have similar  strict surrogacy laws  nebraska and louisiana michigan would be  the riskiest state to ever try and do a  surrogacy contract  michigan family law attorney barbara  holmier said the myers may have been  able to avoid this  if they went to another state it's also  very expensive to go out of state hire  lawyers and find surrogates and do  everything else right to to go out of  state do you think the law in michigan  needs to be updated  yeah i do since they legalize gay  marriage too this is a much bigger issue  there are a lot of couples  who want to have kids and they need to  use surrogates to do that  to adopt their children the myers will  now have to go through months of home  inspections  paperwork and even an fbi background  check  they're speaking out to help others we  just want the law to be updated our hope  is that  we will be the last family in michigan  in this situation where we are being  denied our own biological children  the myers currently cannot get the twins  on their health insurance  the babies are still in the newborn icu  but they are doing well  and will hopefully go home to their  parents and big sister corin soon  we reached out to a clerk for both  judges but we have not heard back  tony it's very strange one thing after  another we'll see if the political arena  picks it up nikki thank you very much

